From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:04:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] security/memory: Let an option turn off clearing DRAM on boot

SECURITY_CLEAR_DRAM_ON_REGULAR_BOOT clears all the memory on every boot
that is not an S3 resume. It protects what the previous OS left in
memory, at a cost that grows with the memory installed: 1.7 seconds with
32 GiB on a Haswell ThinkPad W541, most of the time coreboot takes to
boot it.

Read the option "clear_dram_on_boot", on by default, so that a setup
menu can offer the choice at runtime. Boards without the option, or
without an option backend, keep clearing it as before.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/security/memory/Kconfig  | 3 +++
 src/security/memory/memory.c | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/security/memory/Kconfig b/src/security/memory/Kconfig
index d3dec043d..ded2b280c 100644
--- a/src/security/memory/Kconfig
+++ b/src/security/memory/Kconfig
@@ -19,4 +19,7 @@ config SECURITY_CLEAR_DRAM_ON_REGULAR_BOOT
 	  This increases boot time depending on the amount of DRAM
 	  installed.
 
+	  With an option backend, the option "clear_dram_on_boot" can
+	  turn it off at runtime (it defaults to on).
+
 endmenu #Memory initialization
diff --git a/src/security/memory/memory.c b/src/security/memory/memory.c
index c4f3bdd68..07ca0c028 100644
--- a/src/security/memory/memory.c
+++ b/src/security/memory/memory.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
 
+#include <option.h>
 #include <security/intel/txt/txt.h>
 #include <stdbool.h>
 
@@ -12,7 +13,8 @@
  */
 bool security_clear_dram_request(void)
 {
-	if (CONFIG(SECURITY_CLEAR_DRAM_ON_REGULAR_BOOT))
+	if (CONFIG(SECURITY_CLEAR_DRAM_ON_REGULAR_BOOT) &&
+	    get_uint_option("clear_dram_on_boot", true))
 		return true;
 
 	if (CONFIG(INTEL_TXT) && intel_txt_memory_has_secrets())
-- 
